ER-Diagram Description

The AI StudyBuddy system uses six main entities: User, Study Material, Summary, Flashcard, Quiz, and Study Plan. These entities are represented as separate MongoDB collections and are connected using ObjectId references.

The User entity stores the details of registered students and administrators. Each user is uniquely identified using the _id field. A user can create and manage multiple study materials.

The Study Material entity stores learning content uploaded by users. The userId field establishes a relationship between the study material and its owner. Each study material can be processed by the AI service to generate summaries, flashcards, and quizzes.

The Summary entity stores AI-generated summarized content. It contains both userId and materialId, which identify the user and the source study material.

The Flashcard entity stores AI-generated question-and-answer pairs. Multiple flashcards can be created from a single study material.

The Quiz entity stores AI-generated multiple-choice questions. Each quiz is associated with a specific user and study material. The questions field contains the generated questions, options, and correct answers.

The Study Plan entity stores personalized study schedules generated for users. It contains the study plan details and the user's examination date.

The overall relationship can be represented as one-to-many (1:N) relationships. One user can have multiple study materials, summaries, flashcards, quizzes, and study plans. A study material can also have multiple summaries, flashcards, and quizzes.

